+# 2026-10-25
+
+## ARM brief 4: natural C reaches the target preheader
+
+Tags: #08000430 #arm #matching #natural-c
+
+Traced twenty-seven natural sources of 08000430 against the pinned reference
+through expansion, CSE1, GCSE, loop motion, CSE2, scheduling and allocation.
+Output parameters delay constant knowledge past CSE1; a separate count-pointer
+initializer blocks adjacent-copy reversal. One retained source has the target
+cursor/count priorities, sl/r8 assignment and preheader order, but the test
+address is still merged and rematerialized too early into ip. No exact natural
+match or coverage gain (0.00 percentage points). Restored the incoming unit;
+acmp zero and all six functions MATCH. Full local log: ARM kit `REPORT4.md`;
+[notes](../../notes/arm-clean-slate_2026-10-25.md).
+
+## Natural ARM cursor RTL investigation
+
+Tags: #08000430 #arm #matching #natural-c
+
+BRIEF3's 08000430 investigation logged 92 trials without an exact natural
+match (0 percentage-point exact-code gain). Distinct address expressions and
+multiword SUBREG destinations bypass GCSE PRE, but retain arithmetic or spill
+the carrier. The existing four-difference direct-global draft still fails
+the production checker with its guard removed. Restored the genuine pinned
+incoming source and verified acmp zero plus whole-unit MATCH. No full build,
+commit or push. See [notes](../../notes/arm-rtl-round3_2026-10-25.md) and the
+local `build/arm_kit/REPORT3.md`.
+
+## Natural ARM rewrite follow-up
+
+Tags: #08000430 #arm #matching #natural-c
+
+Sixty more natural variants of 08000430 leave the best unchanged at 89.1%
+normalized sequence similarity (+0.0 percentage points in this follow-up).
+Natural early queue handles reproduce base-first indexing, but preserve the
+base in a register or spill slot instead of reconstructing it inside the loop.
+Compiler dumps identify the initializer's two sched1 sets and lack of constant
+REG_EQUIV as the failure in the function-scope example. Palette abstractions
+and cursor helpers do not improve the result. Incoming source restored; no
+exact coverage gained. See [notes](../../notes/arm-natural_2026-10-25.md).
+
+## Natural ARM sprite-builder exploration
+
+Tags: #08000430 #arm #matching #natural-c
+
+A whole-function rewrite of 08000430 explored 58 natural C variants using the
+Boktai 2 references. Best normalized sequence similarity: 89.1% (+16.5
+percentage points from the supplied clean baseline), with 89 instruction
+differences. No exact coverage gained or source integration performed.
+Production compiler comparison and 20,000 randomized host state comparisons
+passed their respective checks. The remaining source question is chiefly
+Boktai 3's separate tile-request base/index calculation and its resulting
+allocation and scheduling. See [notes](../../notes/arm-natural_2026-10-25.md).
