+# Natural ARM cursor RTL investigation
+
+Tags: #08000430 #arm #matching #natural-c
+
+Followed `build/arm_kit/BRIEF3.md` after reading its predecessors. No natural
+match; exact-code gain is 0 percentage points. The 92 logged trials include
+78 compiled comparisons and 14 compilation failures. Full experiment table,
+compiler findings, validity exclusions and production-check logs are recorded
+in `build/arm_kit/REPORT3.md`; sources and RTL remain in the ignored kit.
+
+Reproduced p6u's 28 differences and the diagnostic zero obtained by disabling
+four GCSE PRE deletions. The closest new representation uses an array end
+pointer and backs up one element: five masked instruction differences, one
+extra instruction, and a production MISMATCH. Distinct address expressions
+avoid PRE, but local allocation cannot fold the symbolic cancellation away.
+
+Two-word cursor contexts produce genuine SUBREG destinations that GCSE skips.
+CSE2 annotates the hoisted cursor extraction correctly, giving priority 739
+and sl. The multiword carrier lacks a whole-register equivalence and spills,
+leaving extra instructions/frame storage. Ordinary register declarations,
+field ordering, inline member staging and useful cursor/EWRAM contexts do not
+remove it. Scalar wrappers, output setters, alternate return modes, libcall
+expansion probes and lazy initialization provide no accepted alternative.
+
+The existing direct-global draft remains four instructions off, solely the
+two cursor-preheader load positions. Its NONMATCHING guard was removed for
+the production comparison: MISMATCH, 22 differing bytes, four realigned
+instructions. An initial check with that guard still present exercised the
+assembly fallback and is explicitly excluded from candidate acceptance.
+
+Restored `src/iwram_code.c` byte-for-byte from the genuine incoming pinned
+snapshot, as BRIEF3 requires: acmp zero and whole-unit `tools/check.py` MATCH
+(4364 bytes). No net source change, full build, commit or push. Resuming needs
+a new scalar assignment form hidden from GCSE but recoverable as a noted
+copy after loop motion, or a way to eliminate the multiword carrier.
